{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And you shall love.</b> And after we have no other Elohim but Him alone, you are obligated to love Him, for we have no other Elohim." "<b>With all your heart and with all your soul.</b> The heart is the intellect, and it is a designation for the rational spirit, for it is the first chariot. So too חכם לב קונה לב (Proverbs 16:23)." "<b>Your soul.</b> It is the spirit that is in the body, and it is the desiring one, and its power is seen in the liver." "<b>Me'odekha.</b> For the reason of מאד מאד. The sense: love Him greatly, with all that you can, and let the love be complete in the heart."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:22:32.992447529Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}